accouplement:
n. The act of coupling, or the state of being coupled;
   union.
n. That which couples, as a tie or brace.

questors:
plural of questor
n. An officer who had the management of the public treasure;
   a receiver of taxes, tribute, etc.; treasurer of state.

summoner:
v. t. One who summons; one who cites by authority;
   specifically, a petty officer formerly employed to summon persons to
   appear in court; an apparitor.
